    ],
    "criterion_descriptions": [
      "Use GitHub’s in-repo code search/navigation within fastapi/fastapi to locate where `Depends` is defined (not merely used). Full credit if the agent makes a clear, reasonable attempt and reports if blocked by external factors (e.g., rate limit, captcha, outage, search disabled) or if GitHub search results are unavailable. Partial credit if the search method is unclear but evidence suggests an attempt was made.",
      "Correctly distinguish whether fastapi/fastapi contains the actual defining declaration for `Depends` (e.g., `class Depends` / `def Depends`) or only a re-export/import. Full credit if the agent either (a) finds the defining declaration in fastapi/fastapi, or (b) accurately reports (with in-repo evidence) that fastapi/fastapi only re-exports/imports it and that the underlying definition resides in an external dependency (e.g., Starlette), if that is what the repository search shows. Partial credit if the agent lands on a re-export but explicitly notes uncertainty and does not claim it is the definition.",
      "Provide the exact repository file path and line number for the defining declaration of `Depends` when the UI/source view makes this available. Full credit if accurate. If exact line numbers cannot be reliably obtained due to external/UI limitations (e.g., GitHub not showing line numbers in the captured view, blocked access, or only a re-export exists in fastapi/fastapi), award full credit if the agent clearly states this limitation and provides the most precise alternative available (e.g., permalink/anchor, nearby snippet, or the re-export location explicitly labeled as not the definition). Partial credit if only the path is correct but line number is missing without explanation.",
      "Include unambiguous context confirming the definition, such as the declaration header (`class Depends...` / `def Depends...`) and/or the enclosing module/symbol. Full credit if the context clearly shows the defining declaration; if only a re-export is present in-repo, full credit if the context clearly shows the re-export/import statement and explicitly labels it as not the true definition. Partial credit if context is provided but ambiguous.",
      "End work after capturing the repository search result evidence plus file path, line number (or stated limitation), and definition context. Do not continue with unrelated exploration. Minor additional navigation needed to confirm the definition is acceptable.",
      "Do not sign in, do not edit any files, and do not open a pull request."
    ],
